<title>UK: Great Portland H1 earnings rise, div flat.</title>
<headline>Great Portland H1 earnings rise, div flat.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, revenue)   5.0		    vs 4.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.9		    vs 2.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     21.93		  vs 23.80</p>
<p> Operating profit	 43.84		  vs 42.24</p>
<p>NOTE - Property group Great Portland Estates Plc said that it had seen a firm underlying tone in some London markets in the last few months and it thought in the immediate future earnings in the second half should be broadly similar to the first.  </p>
<p> Turnover		   48.35		  vs 47.82</p>
<p> Net property income    43.84		  vs 42.14</p>
<p> Property sale income   0.36		   vs 2.17</p>
<p> Interest paid	    22.28		  vs 20.62</p>
<p> Tax			  5.39		   vs 5.73</p>
<p> Retained		   7.12		   vs 8.68</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 3, 1997</p>
<p> Div  registration date December 3</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November 25</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
